godotengine/godot/issues/123514#issuecomment-5679325013","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123514","id":5679325013,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUoOfVQ","user":{"login":"JulienLavocat","id":10382496,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzgyNDk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10382496?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienLavocat","html_url":"https://github.com/JulienLavocat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienLavocat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienLavocat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienLavocat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienLavocat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienLavocat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienLavocat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienLavocat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienLavocat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienLavocat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-15T11:20:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T11:20:18Z","body":"Fair enough @AThousandShips , I understand.\n\nFor the sake of discussion, here are my findings and thoughts on the issue:\n- Active objects is indeed easy enough and should expose the same value as GodotPhysics does\n- Jolt doesn't directly expose the number of collision pairs but it can be done by counting them using `JoltContactListener3D::OnContactAdded` and `JoltContactListener3D::OnContactPersisted`, although these would be narrow-phase contacts (which differs from GodotPhysics)\n- Island count cannot be implemented, it would require an upstream change in Jolt to expose this value.\n\nI rely on these counters to debug performance in my game since its physics heavy. I'm still more than happy to implement this, pending 